    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1220">

                <pb facs="1283" n="1271" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg1271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894a.01/7–1944</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Office of European Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director of
                        the Civil Affairs Division, War Department</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hilldring</hi>)<anchor n="70" xml:id="d1220-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-21">July 21, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General Hilldring</hi>: I am transmitting
                    herewith a series of papers prepared by the State Department on “Military
                    Government <pb facs="1284" n="1272" xml:id="pg1272"/> in Formosa” relating to
                    political and policy questions presented by the War and Navy Departments.<anchor
                        n="71" xml:id="d1220-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>These papers are identical with those which were transmitted earlier with the
                    indication that they represent the informal views of experts in the Department.
                    The papers have since been formally approved at the policy level and may now be
                    regarded as the present views of the Department of State, subject, however, to
                    such modifications as may be necessary in the light of future
                        developments.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d1220-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James Clement Dunn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1220-f1" n="70" type="source" xml:id="d1220-f1-content">
